{
  "frames": [
    {
      "frame_number": 1,
      "caption": "I entered the Spouter-Inn and, after much pondering and throwing open the little window, I made out the smoke-dark painting: a half-foundered ship and an exasperated whale springing upon her three masts.",
      "caption_zone": "top_left",
      "dialogue": [],
      "dialogue_layout": [],
      "source_image": "work/mobydick/graphic_novel/action_spine_v3/chapter_003/final_frames/frame_001.png",
      "lettered_image": "work/mobydick/graphic_novel/action_spine_v3/chapter_003/dialogue_prototype_lettered_frames/frame_001.png",
      "frame_box": {
        "x1": 0,
        "y1": 0,
        "x2": 1536,
        "y2": 1024
      }
    },
    {
      "frame_number": 2,
      "caption": "I sought the landlord for a room, and being told the house was full, I consented\u2014if the harpooneer were not decidedly objectionable\u2014to share a blanket rather than wander further on so bitter a night.",
      "caption_zone": "bottom_center",
      "dialogue": [],
      "dialogue_layout": [],
      "source_image": "work/mobydick/graphic_novel/action_spine_v3/chapter_003/final_frames/frame_002.png",
      "lettered_image": "work/mobydick/graphic_novel/action_spine_v3/chapter_003/dialogue_prototype_lettered_frames/frame_002.png",
      "frame_box": {
        "x1": 0,
        "y1": 0,
        "x2": 1536,
        "y2": 1024
      }
    },
    {
      "frame_number": 3,
      "caption": "I changed my mind about that harpooneer, chose the bench, and soon learned that knots, a foot too short, and the meeting draughts would never do\u2014while the landlord kept chuckling that the fellow was out \u2018selling his head.\u2019",
      "caption_zone": "top_right",
      "dialogue": [],
      "dialogue_layout": [],
      "source_image": "work/mobydick/graphic_novel/action_spine_v3/chapter_003/final_frames/frame_003.png",
      "lettered_image": "work/mobydick/graphic_novel/action_spine_v3/chapter_003/dialogue_prototype_lettered_frames/frame_003.png",
      "frame_box": {
        "x1": 0,
        "y1": 0,
        "x2": 1536,
        "y2": 1024
      }
    },
    {
      "frame_number": 4,
      "caption": "Provoked by his bamboozling yarn of selling his head, I demanded the truth, and heard it plain\u2014embalmed New Zealand heads, peddled on a Saturday night.",
      "caption_zone": "bottom_left",
      "dialogue": [
        {
          "speaker": "Peter Coffin",
          "text": "He went out peddling. Maybe he can\u2019t sell his head.",
          "balloon_zone": "top_left",
          "speaker_position": "right",
          "anchor": "mouth",
          "anchor_x_ratio": 0.76,
          "anchor_y_ratio": 0.34
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Ishmael",
          "text": "Peddling his head around town?",
          "balloon_zone": "top_center",
          "speaker_position": "center_left",
          "anchor": "mouth",
          "anchor_x_ratio": 0.39,
          "anchor_y_ratio": 0.27
        },
        {
          "speaker": "Peter Coffin",
          "text": "Embalmed New Zealand heads. He\u2019s sold all but one.",
          "balloon_zone": "top_right",
          "speaker_position": "right",
          "anchor": "mouth",
          "anchor_x_ratio": 0.76,
