    },
    {
      "frame_number": 5,
      "caption": "Seeing it was Sunday and he\u2019d come to anchor elsewhere, I let the landlord lead me to the prodigious bed; I eyed the room and the harpooneer\u2019s outlandish gear, then turned in.",
      "caption_zone": "top_center",
      "dialogue": [],
      "dialogue_layout": [],
      "source_image": "work/mobydick/graphic_novel/action_spine_v3/chapter_003/final_frames/frame_005.png",
      "lettered_image": "work/mobydick/graphic_novel/action_spine_v3/chapter_003/dialogue_prototype_lettered_frames/frame_005.png",
      "frame_box": {
        "x1": 0,
        "y1": 0,
        "x2": 1586,
        "y2": 992
      }
    },
    {
      "frame_number": 6,
      "caption": "Dozing at last, I saw the harpooneer come in with a New Zealand head, undress to tattooed squares, set a little wooden idol in the fireplace, burn shavings and biscuit, and sing out in strange gutturals.",
      "caption_zone": "bottom_right",
      "dialogue": [],
      "dialogue_layout": [],
      "source_image": "work/mobydick/graphic_novel/action_spine_v3/chapter_003/final_frames/frame_006.png",
      "lettered_image": "work/mobydick/graphic_novel/action_spine_v3/chapter_003/dialogue_prototype_lettered_frames/frame_006.png",
      "frame_box": {
        "x1": 0,
        "y1": 0,
        "x2": 1536,
        "y2": 1024
      }
    },
    {
      "frame_number": 7,
      "caption": "Then, tomahawk-pipe between his teeth, he sprang into bed with me; I sang out, and the landlord burst in with a light to swear the harpooneer, Queequeg, wouldn\u2019t harm a hair of my head.",
      "caption_zone": "top_right",
      "dialogue": [],
      "dialogue_layout": [],
      "source_image": "work/mobydick/graphic_novel/action_spine_v3/chapter_003/final_frames/frame_007.png",
      "lettered_image": "work/mobydick/graphic_novel/action_spine_v3/chapter_003/dialogue_prototype_lettered_frames/frame_007.png",
      "frame_box": {
        "x1": 0,
        "y1": 0,
        "x2": 1536,
        "y2": 1024
      }
    },
    {
      "frame_number": 8,
      "caption": "Better sleep with a sober cannibal than a drunken Christian, thought I; he stashed the tomahawk-pipe, I turned in again, and never slept better in my life.",
      "caption_zone": "bottom_center",
      "dialogue": [],
      "dialogue_layout": [],
